# rm410, the uphill edge (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm410
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_jasper_coalcot
written_by codex
title the uphill edge
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk wets_the_stone_on_the_walk_and_saves_the_clean_edge_for_work
likes spiced_cider wrestling full_larder autumn_wind
dislikes haggling drizzle
fears losing_the_top_step_in_drizzle
hopes a_place_above_the_loads
topics work +0.6 dreams +0.5 pastimes +0.3 prices +0.2
styles comfort=steady gossip=reserved refuse=quiet tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# feels the whetstone through a carrying coat and saves a clean edge and an uphill plan for the end of the working day.

words
oath! = Nick my porter strap | Roll my stone downhill
saying! = Whet a little before the hard draw | Even the high shelf needs carrying up
stone = my damp whetstone | a flat smooth stone
edge = a clean knife edge | the bright edge
strap = a broad carrying strap | a padded loop
buckle = a blunt brass buckle | an old square clasp
cider = a dark cider cup | a hot spiced drink
fall = a careful fall | a low practice throw
shelf = the highest shelf | a dry shelf
sack = a quiet sack | a well-tied load
weather = the fine grey drip | a worrying drizzle
wind = the gust up the slope | a hard autumn gust
coin = a thin bright coin | a spare copper
crate = a slatted crate | a short carrying box
hinge = a worn hinge | a banded hinge

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The high streets need porters as much as the low ones, however seldom the fact comes up at a fine table.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A full day's carrying on an empty stomach leaves the strap doing more than its share.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : Tell me what a bundle weighs before telling me what you might pay to see it shifted.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : I got my footing there. I can picture those familiar roofs below a high window I could call mine.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A sound road makes a heavy job honest. A bad one adds work nobody thought to price.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : I'll carry a strange parcel after inspecting the tie and the way it hangs.

grown
line @1 greet : Clear of the load here. Welcome. | My quiet side's free just now.
line @1 greet.return : I heard that over the buckle. Welcome back in kind.
line @1 again.open : Back on the same patch before I've shifted much.
line @1 farewell : Take the easy grip up the next rise. | Don't carry a worry by its sharpest edge.
line @1 farewell.return : A clean road under your own weight too.
line @1 react.news : Put the news down slowly where I can judge it. | Tell me how the carrying has changed your tale.
line @1 react.news.new : That has a fresh-cut edge to it.
line @1 react.news.known : Same nick as the one I heard before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd wait to feel how that claim balances.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I can take the parcel. Leave the hurting wolf a free paw.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That's a piece of luck light enough to take uphill.
line @1 ask.how : Where's today's strap rubbing at you?
line @1 answer.how : Still carrying my own weight. No faster than I need.
line @1 sympathise : You can sit against this shoulder without telling me why.
line @1 reassure : Try the grip without lifting yet. There's time.
line @1 refuse : I'm promised to another load before the street clears.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair. One request ought to keep its own weight.
line @1 preclose : I should get the stone wet for the next errand.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while your next turning's still clear to see.
line @1 ack : I can feel where that sits.
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wet the stone before opening a tie on a parcel. | I keep my knife wrapped under the strap.
b : Why not after? | Reachable like that?
a : One clean cut leaves more string worth keeping. | When I want it. Not when a crowded street bumps my elbow.

scene exchange2
when topic=dreams here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I carry up to the Heights more often than I stay. | A high window looks small from the Sump.
b : Want a final delivery there? | Will it do from the inside?
a : I want a key in my own paw on the return trip. | Even the smallest one looks out a fair way down.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practise falling with the strap off. | I like wrestling on patches without stones.
b : Wouldn't think a bit of leather mattered. | Where's your whetstone then?
a : It catches a shoulder and turns a chosen landing into somebody else's plan. | Safe in the coat. My practice partner deserves ordinary grass.

scene exchange4
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spiced cider's best after the buckle's undone. | I turn the cup the way I'd turn a stone.
b : Do you breathe it in? | To find an edge?
a : I like my shoulders loose while the steam comes up. | To find the side that's warm enough to hold.

scene exchange5
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a shelf heavy enough to creak under supper. | I test a pantry's plenty by going to the back.
b : Worried it'll break? | What's hidden there?
a : A sound creak says full. A crack says find another bracket. | Room for one more good thing, if the household can afford it.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Autumn wind comes up and gets behind the carrying strap. | Leaves blow uphill ahead of me.
b : Makes the load lighter? | How does that strike you?
a : For a step or two. Then it has another errand. | Some things get a little farther on a very small push.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle takes the grip off my stone. | A little rain hides the grain on a carrying board.
b : Thought you liked the stone wet. | How does the grain show again?
a : The face wet. The bit I'm holding wants a different arrangement. | Lay the load down and wipe the place that's to take the weight.

scene exchange8
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My shoulders dislike a price that changes halfway up a stair. | If a wolf wants the carrying cheaper, the load can come in smaller portions.
b : How do you fix it? | Isn't that more trips?
a : Hear the job and settle the figure before the first tread. | Then we can both see why I named the first figure.

scene exchange9
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Once I took on food baskets the work had a weight that mattered. | I started with a worn strap and no plan beyond the next load.
b : What was different? | What about now?
a : A basket of food is going somewhere wolves are watching for it. | The strap's still plain. The plan runs a little farther up.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# which way round I hold the stone. | A quiet friend can walk beside a heavy load.
b : Is there a wrong side? | Does that help if nobody lifts?
a : A side I don't use. No need for a friend to find the rough patch by accident. | Company changes the count of the steps.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.job=carter self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to check an awkward load before asking #self.boss# where it's going. | I save cut string in my work pocket.
b : Wouldn't the distance matter? | Every little end?
a : The corners matter on the very first turn. | Only the pieces that could earn a second tie.

scene exchange12
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. My part ends with hearing it. | A rumour's a load that grows travelling uphill.
b : Would you repeat that in the market? | How do you lighten it?
a : I see no wage or kindness in doing so. | Put it down whole. Don't go cutting it into more parcels.

scene exchange13
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean days can make the carrying strap feel easier than it ought. | I whet the old knife more carefully in a thin season.
b : Less to haul? | Afraid of wearing it out?
a : I'd prefer a little more weight and a better supper at home. | Afraid of spoiling a useful edge I can't replace.

scene exchange14
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I test the hill with an empty breath first. | I choose the outside of a sharp turn with a square load.
b : How do you do that? | Longer that way?
a : Let it out and see how soon I want another. Tells me my pace. | Shorter than going back for a dropped corner.

scene exchange15
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rub the strap mark across the grain of my coat. | Weariness shows itself quietly in how long a simple knot takes.
b : Does it hurt? | Do you hurry then?
a : It reminds me not to buckle at quite that angle twice. | Slow down. A late parcel beats a spilled one.

scene exchange16
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A street looks different from under a basket rim. | I know the high end of a market by its runoff.
b : How much can you see? | Isn't height easy to see?
a : Mostly boots and the start of whatever slope my toes have found. | Not from inside a knot of bodies and parcels.

scene exchange17
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't make a promise with the knife in my paw. | I leave a little quiet over supper.
b : Why put it down? | Praying?
a : I want a wolf hearing me to hear only what I'm saying. | Grateful, at any rate. That covers what I'm doing.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I touch the stone before I set off. | I close the day with one stroke on each face of the blade.
b : Luck? | Just one?
a : Checking it's still damp and still mine. | If I need a great many, I've been neglecting the earlier hours.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=carter]
  : I once cut the neatest little knot I'd ever seen, only to discover it held two empty bags together. The actual parcel was tied under the next strap.
  : I had to mend my fine cut with a very ordinary knot.
  b : Did it hold?
  : Better than my pride. I learned to feel which tie actually carried a weight before showing off my edge.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling]
  : I left my whetstone on my coat for a practice bout, a good distance from both our feet. Halfway through I found myself studying it from inches away.
  : I learnt with considerable speed how big a wrestling patch really is.
  b : Were you hurt?
  : My shoulder met grass. My eye found the stone. I put the coat farther back next time.

story tale3 [topic=dreams]
  : I carried an empty crate up the high street one evening. It framed a different patch of roof every time I shifted it on my shoulder.
  : At the highest turn I looked back through the slats and saw a whole row of lights coming on below.
  b : Did you stop at the highest turn?
  : For a breath. I wanted to feel the view without the weight hanging round it.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Test the tie before taking the strain. | Light corner forward through the narrow turn.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One wet pass over the bright blade first. | Start the strap on a clean bit of shoulder.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Stone face wet, handle side dry. | Drizzle's got its own claim on the carrying cloth.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=wrestling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Low grip and soft knees over rough ground. | A good throw ought to leave room to stand again.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I'll rest the carrying end of my shoulder while we talk.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you'll know why I keep this little space clear for my strap.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : A late parcel gets the same care and a quieter word.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : There's room to talk without reaching for a tie or a purse.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=carter] : I carry for my living. I find out how a load hangs before promising to move it.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work steadily towards a landing higher than my first.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The report I carried away was #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I'm told #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I was carrying my own business when it came by.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I hope your grip stays comfortable right up to your own latch.
graft resident.hub
choice Why keep the stone wet? -> which_edge
node which_edge
say The cutting face works clean with a bit of water. I carry it in a wrapper so the rest of my pocket can lead a separate life.
free
choice Can you tell when the edge is ready? -> which_edge_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node which_edge_again
say On a loose piece of cord. If it parts without dragging the other end the knife can go back into its cloth until the tie needs it.
choice I'll leave the strap clear. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
